  "_comment": "India Aadhaar Secure QR (UIDAI). The QR is a decimal integer; its bytes are zlib/gzip-compressed; fields are separated by 0xFF; the last 256 bytes are an RSA-2048 PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-256 signature by UIDAI over everything before them. The QR carries only the last 4 digits of the Aadhaar number, so uniqueness uses last4 + birth date + gender + a hash of the enrolment photo, which UIDAI embeds unchanged in every QR it issues for that person. Keys: UIDAI's offline e-KYC signing certificates (copied from anon-aadhaar, MIT, packages/react/src/publicKeys.ts); add the current one from uidai.gov.in when UIDAI rotates it.",
